course: dictionary
lesson: 5863
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and manage is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning to choose. «I managed to finish the race» means you succeeded in doing something hard.
explain: «She manages a shop» is different: it means she is in charge of the shop. «Manage your time» means control or look after your time. Read the whole sentence first, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «We'll manage» means we will cope with what we have, so it does not mean the same as «I managed to finish the race». Same word, different job.
fact: Manage can mean to succeed in doing something difficult, as in «I managed to finish the race».
fact: Manage can mean to be in charge of a business, team or people, as in «She manages a shop».
fact: Manage can mean to control or look after something, as in «manage your time» and «manage money».
fact: Manage can mean to cope or get by with what you have, as in «We'll manage».
fact: The context tells you which meaning is right, so always read the words around the word.
exercise: «I managed to finish the race.» What does managed mean here? | *Succeeded in doing something hard | Lost my way | Walked away from it | Ran faster than everyone else
exercise: «She manages a shop.» What does manages mean here? | Is afraid of | *Is in charge of | Is closing for the day | Buys cheap things for
exercise: Ben says «We'll manage» means someone will give us lots of help. Is he right? | *Yes, it means someone will do it for us | No, it means we will cope with what we have | No, it means we will go home | Yes, it means the shop is closing
test: «Manage your time» during a test. What does manage mean here? | To be in charge of a team | To sing loudly | To cook a meal | *To control or look after
test: «He managed to save £5 a week.» What does managed mean here? | *Succeeded in doing it | Spent all his money on sweets | Lost £5 in a shop | Was given £5 by his mum
exam: Which sentence uses manage to mean cope with what you have? | «Manage your feelings.» | *«We'll manage with the food we have.» | «She manages a team of ten people.» | «I managed to climb the hill.»
